  "answer_markdown": "To achieve both **automatic user joining** and **sign-in without separate password credentials**, the following mechanisms and requirements apply based on Mistral's plans and verified domain policies:\n\n1. **Automatic user joining (Organization membership)**\n   - Supported by **Email domain authentication** (no plan restriction mentioned, but requires a [verified domain][5]).\n   - Users with an email matching the verified domain can join automatically via the [Join Organization] link [5].\n   - However, users still **create and manage their own email/password credentials**—this does not eliminate password requirements [5].\n\n2. **Sign-in without separate password credentials (SSO)**\n   - Supported by **SAML SSO** (requires an **Enterprise plan** and a [verified domain][1]).\n   - Users with an email matching the verified domain are **automatically redirected to the IdP** for authentication, bypassing password fields [1].\n   - On first sign-in, Mistral **provisions the user account automatically** in the Organization [1].\n   - **No password is required** for sign-in after SSO is configured [1].\n\n### Key Requirements for Each Mechanism\n- **Email domain authentication**:\n  - Requires at least **one verified domain** [5].\n  - Does **not** eliminate password requirements for sign-in [5].\n\n- **SAML SSO**:\n  - Requires an **Enterprise plan** [1].\n  - Requires at least **one verified domain** [1].\n  - Enables **passwordless sign-in** via corporate IdP [1].\n\n### Combined Solution\nFor **both automatic joining and passwordless sign-in**, **SAML SSO (Enterprise plan)** is the only supported mechanism. Email domain authentication alone does not eliminate password requirements [5].\n\n> **Note**: SAML SSO uses **SAML 2.0** and does not support OpenID Connect (OIDC) [1].",
  "citations": [
    {
      "n": 1,
      "quote": "SAML single sign-on (SSO) lets members of your Organization **sign in with your corporate identity provider** (IdP). Any user with an email address that matches your verified domain is redirected to your configured IdP to authenticate."
