  "answer_markdown": "When you retry failed records in a batch run using `retry_failed_records()`, the following happens to the run's evaluators and results in the console:\n\n- The SDK identifies and reprocesses only the records with a status of `\"error\"` (failed generation or scoring) [1].\n\n- The successful results from the retry are **patched into the original run** in Studio, updating the existing results in place [1].\n\n- If the original run included **run evaluators** (evaluators that operate on the full set of results), their scores are **recomputed** with the updated data after the failed records are retried [1].\n\n- The original run in the console remains a **single, updated run**—no duplicate runs are created, and no manual cleanup is required [1].\n\nThis ensures that the evaluation results stay cohesive and reflect the latest state after retries.",
